        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f0858b1d-5f33-57ce-9366-437b15c278e2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Isochrysis galbana\n- Concepts: haptophytes, bivalve larvae, cosmetic properties, hair-growth properties, extractants\n- Chemicals: isopropyl alcohol, propan-2-ol, dimethyl carbinol, hexane, ethyl acetate, ethanol, water, methanol, isopropanol\n\nFacts:\n- Isochrysis galbana is a species of haptophytes.\n- Isochrysis galbana is an outstanding food for various bivalve larvae.\n- Extracts of Isochrysis galbana are said to have cosmetic and hair-growth properties when prepared with hexane, ethyl acetate, ethanol, water, methanol, or isopropanol.\n- Isopropyl alcohol has the IUPAC name propan-2-ol and is also called dimethyl carbinol.\n- The source states that isopropyl alcohol is incorrectly called isopropanol.\n- The source gives chemical formula representations for isopropyl alcohol as CHO, CHOH, CHCHOHCH, and sometimes i-PrOH.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d9f05ab2-f66b-5731-93d0-a5798e6a7c7f",
